In Java unit tests where the explicit action under test is calling `close()` on an `AutoCloseable` resource, do not wrap the resource in a try-with-resources block. Wrapping it executes `close()` twice, which violates the Arrange-Act-Assert structure and is unnecessary.

```java
  void close_whenUninitialized_allowsSubsequentInitialization() {
    LoggingOpenTelemetryProvider provider =
        new LoggingOpenTelemetryProvider(OpenTelemetryOptions.builder().build());
    provider.close();
    OpenTelemetry openTelemetry = provider.getOpenTelemetry();

    assertThat(openTelemetry).isNotNull();
  }
